nodecode-nowstamp is a rewrite of zakiyys's zakiyys/hermes-nowstamp:

  https://github.com/zakiyys/hermes-nowstamp
  commit 26148cca897f0798ca2cfc035e9eb2e00349bcf8
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Zakiyys (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the whole reading -- the timezone-aware clock with its weekday, its
UTC offset and the strftime format setting, English and Bahasa Indonesia
weekday names, the gap since the conversation last moved and the words it is
said in ("5 min ago", "yesterday 19:37", a calendar comparison rather than a
count of hours), the same reading on demand through the now tool and /now, and
the opt-in tool-result stamp with its interval, which here rides the :TOOL
point rather than a first-string-wins transform hook. The grace under failure
is the plugin's: a reading that cannot be built falls back to this machine's
own zone, and a stamp that fails leaves the tool result untouched.

Left out: the hook placement. The plugin appended its line to the user message
of every request through a Hermes-only pre_llm_call hook, recorded reply times
through post_llm_call, and kept its table of last instants in the host's plugin
state; a cell has one standing context seam -- the harness section the engine
reads at a turn's first request and freezes for that turn's rounds -- so the
reading is per turn here, and the table of last instants is a small file of
this home (nowstamp/state.tsv, capped at the plugin's 200 sessions) so a gap
still survives a restart. Also left out: hermes_time, the Hermes runtime
module the plugin imported for its timezone resolver, replaced by this machine's
own tz database; and the plugin's YAML settings file, replaced by the cell's
config section. The now tool, /now and the (help :nowstamp) topic are
additions, not part of the original.
